{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Common.AntiInvolutionPalindrome","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Common.AntiInvolutionPalindrome","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AntiInvolutionPalindrome.first_moment_zero_of_antiInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AntiInvolutionPalindrome.first_moment_zero_of_antiInvolution","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/AntiInvolutionPalindrome.lean#L54-L77","doc":"**First moment vanishes** — the algebraic form of `P'(1) = 0`, i.e. the\nbar-even `O((q−1)²)` rigidity: the derivative of `Σ w i · q^{e i}` at `q = 1` is\n`Σ w i · e i`, and under the same anti-invariant involution this is `0`, so the\nq-deformation of the weighted sum has no linear term (its deviation from the\n`q = 1` value starts at second order). This is the exact statement the level-1/2\nalien datum `Δ_{ω₀}` measured as its bar-even q-rigidity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AntiInvolutionPalindrome.palindromic_sum_of_antiInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AntiInvolutionPalindrome.palindromic_sum_of_antiInvolution","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/AntiInvolutionPalindrome.lean#L37-L52","doc":"**Palindromy from an anti-invariant involution.** If `σ` is an involution of\nthe finite set `s`, the weight `w` is `σ`-invariant, and the exponent `e` is\n`σ`-anti-invariant (`e (σ i) = − e i`), then the weighted exponential sum is\ninvariant under `q ↦ q⁻¹`:\n`Σ_{i∈s} w i · q^{e i} = Σ_{i∈s} w i · q^{−e i}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}